From: FieldmouseWorks <burrow@fieldmouse.works>
Subject: [PATCH] submodule--helper: re-validate gitdirs after parallel clone

During `git clone --recurse-submodules --jobs=N`, `update_submodules()`
spawns concurrent `git submodule--helper clone` children. Each child
calls `validate_submodule_git_dir()` before and after its own clone,
which checks whether any ancestor directory inside `.git/modules/` is
already a git directory (`is_git_directory()`).

With sibling submodules whose gitdirs nest (such as `hippo` and
`hippo/hooks` in `t7450-bad-git-dotfiles.sh` test 48), the child cloning
`hippo/hooks` can finish its post-clone `validate_submodule_git_dir()`
while the sibling child cloning `hippo` has not yet created
`.git/modules/hippo/HEAD`. `is_git_directory(".git/modules/hippo")`
then returns 0, so the `hippo/hooks` child succeeds; the `hippo` child
later creates `HEAD` and only checks ancestors of `hippo` (none), so it
succeeds too. `update_submodules()` then proceeds to check out both
submodules without re-checking their gitdirs, bypassing nested gitdir
detection and making `t7450-bad-git-dotfiles.sh` test 48 flake under
load.

Re-validate every freshly cloned submodule's gitdir in
`update_submodules()` after `run_processes_parallel()` finishes and
before checking out any submodule, disabling any nested gitdir by
unlinking its `HEAD` and aborting.

---
--- a/builtin/submodule--helper.c
+++ b/builtin/submodule--helper.c
@@ -2937,6 +2937,47 @@
 		goto cleanup;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Re-validate every freshly cloned submodule's gitdir once all parallel
+	 * clone children have finished. A child for `a/b` can complete its
+	 * post-clone validate_submodule_git_dir() before a sibling child for
+	 * `a` creates `a/HEAD`, so neither child observes the nested gitdir.
+	 * Checking again here before any checkout runs closes that race.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < suc.update_clone_nr; i++) {
+		struct update_clone_data ucd = suc.update_clone[i];
+		struct strbuf sb = STRBUF_INIT;
+
+		if (!ucd.just_cloned)
+			continue;
+
+		if (!the_repository->repository_format_submodule_path_cfg) {
+			repo_git_path_append(the_repository, &sb, "modules/%s",
+					     ucd.sub->name);
+		} else {
+			const char *gitdir;
+			char *key = xstrfmt("submodule.%s.gitdir", ucd.sub->name);
+			int missing = repo_config_get_string_tmp(the_repository,
+								 key, &gitdir);
+			free(key);
+			if (missing)
+				continue;
+			strbuf_addstr(&sb, gitdir);
+		}
+
+		if (validate_submodule_git_dir(sb.buf, ucd.sub->name) < 0) {
+			char *head = xstrfmt("%s/HEAD", sb.buf);
+			unlink(head);
+			free(head);
+			ret = die_message(_("refusing to create/use '%s' in another submodule's git dir. "
+					    "Enabling extensions.submodulePathConfig should fix this."),
+					  sb.buf);
+		}
+		strbuf_release(&sb);
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		goto cleanup;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < suc.update_clone_nr; i++) {
 		struct update_clone_data ucd = suc.update_clone[i];
 		int code = 128;
